From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pessi-v <pessimo@posteo.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:38:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (lilac) qpnp-fg-gen3: do not report capacity 0 after a failed read

The fuel gauge's SRAM access sometimes times out on this board
("wait for mem_grant timed out"), and the capacity read then returns 0
or fails. Userspace takes 0 % as an empty battery and starts an
emergency shutdown. When the read fails, or returns 0 while the battery
voltage is more than 250 mV above the cutoff voltage, report the last
known capacity instead.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-fg-gen3.c |   11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-fg-gen3.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-fg-gen3.c
index afe0c8ed0bf855eedb008ee293db3df1986adc56..039c1d4783c4c2766d5c2eef743e5861201ad730 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-fg-gen3.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-fg-gen3.c
@@ -3925,6 +3925,17 @@ static int fg_psy_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY:
 		rc = fg_get_prop_capacity(fg, &pval->intval);
+		/* lilac: spurious capacity 0 / failed read (flaky FG SRAM access) must not look like
+		 * an empty battery to mce/DSME; keep the last known value while the voltage is healthy. */
+		if (fg->last_soc > 0 && (rc < 0 || pval->intval == 0)) {
+			int vbatt_uv;
+
+			if (rc < 0 || (!fg_get_battery_voltage(fg, &vbatt_uv) &&
+				vbatt_uv > (chip->dt.cutoff_volt_mv + 250) * 1000)) {
+				pval->intval = fg->last_soc;
+				rc = 0;
+			}
+		}
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY_RAW:
 		rc = fg_get_msoc_raw(fg, &pval->intval);
